            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> **Actual result: The uppermost line in the screen shows 2.**\n> \n> **Expected result: The uppermost line in the screen shows 1.**\n\nCould you please elaborate why \"The uppermost line in the screen shows 1\" is the expected result? When I perform the same steps (`:set scrolloff=1`, file content, `:set foldmethod=marker`, put cursor on the fold, type `zb`) in `nvim --clean`, the uppermost line is 2. Do you see the same behavior? If yes, then this is not a 'mini.animate' issue.",
